The foldable iPhone will be Apple's first new form factor since the launch of the 2017 iPhone X. It will have a book-like design, and it will be around 5.5 inches when closed and 7.6 inches when open. It is wider than it is tall, and will be similar to using an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> when unfolded. Since the foldable iPhone is so thin, there are compromises, and it will use <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/touch-id/">Touch ID</a> instead of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a> and it won't have a telephoto camera.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is also going to introduce the Apple Watch Series 12 and Apple Watch Ultra 4, plus there's a possibility we'll see new smart home devices, including the long-rumored home hub, a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> 4K, and an updated <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini</a>.<br/>
<br/>
